  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Kim earned scores of \\(87,\\) \\(83\\) and \\(88\\) on her first three mathematics examinations. If Kim receives a score of \\(90\\) on the fourth exam, then her average will",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "remain the same",
    "B": "increase by \\(1\\)",
    "C": "increase by \\(2\\)",
    "D": "increase by \\(3\\)",
    "E": "increase by \\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "An average is the total score divided by the number of exams. Kim's original average is\n\\[\n\\frac{87+83+88}{3}=\\frac{258}{3}=86.\n\\]\nAfter the fourth exam, her average becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{258+90}{4}=\\frac{348}{4}=87.\n\\]\nThus her average increases by \\(87-86=\\boxed{1}\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
